_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 31
---
order: 31
---
short_label: XI.31
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: Parallelepipedal solids which are on equal bases and of the same height equal one another.
----
proof:

Let the parallelepipedal solids {AE|sAE} and {CF|sCF} of the same height be on equal bases {AB|baseAB} and {CD|baseCD}.

I say that the solid {AE|sAE} equals the solid {CF|sCF}.

First, let the sides which stand up, {HK}, {BE|EB}, {AG}, {LM}, {PQ}, {DF|FD}, {CO}, and {RS}, be at right angles to the bases {AB|baseAB} and {CD|baseCD}. Produce the straight line {RT} in a straight line with {CR}. Construct the angle {TRU|angTRU} equal to the angle {ALB|angALB} at the point {R} on the straight line {RT}. Make {RT} equal to *A,* and {RU} equal to {LB}. Complete the base {RW|pRW} and the solid {XU|sXU}. [!just I.23; I.3; I.31]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="400" height="280" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XI.31 diagram" src="propXI31a.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure for the first case: the solids AE and CF on equal
    // bases, the solid XU built on RT and RU beside CF, then DR and WU
    // produced to Y, aTb drawn through T, and the solids YX and RI.
    //
    // Added, all transparent unless noted: a faceless hexagon on each
    // solid's outline (sAE, sCF, sXU, sXY, sRI, sCI, sYI) to carry the
    // solid's highlight, since a polyhedron draws none; faceless
    // quadrilaterals for the bases and parallelograms the proof names
    // (baseAB, which is also Joyce's HL; baseCD; pRW, also RUWT; pRX, pAM,
    // pLE, pSU, pDT, pYT, pYc, pUV; pRF, the cutting plane), since a filled
    // face would be raised over the figure (#140); the standing edges and
    // lines the proof names (HK, AG, LM, PQ, CO, RS, CR, AL, DY, Tb, Sd, Xc,
    // XV, YW, eV). RU, UW and ab (Joyce's aTb) are solid slide twins over
    // edges of Joyce's faces, hidden at rest (initiallyHidden), so they can
    // be drawn as the construction reaches them. The angles TRU, ALB are
    // markers; ALM, CRS, TRS are right angles. All hidden at rest.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, M, K, C, P, D, all on the
    // given solids. Every other point is derived and listed per slide.
    var AE  = ["G","A","M","K","L","H","B","E","AGKH","ALMG","GKEM","EB","HB","LB"];
    var CF  = ["C","P","D","R","F","Q","O","S","QOCP","QOSF","COSR","FD","PD","RD"];
    var TGT = ["sAE","sCF","baseAB","baseCD","HK","AG","LM","PQ","CO","RS","CR","AL"];
    var GIVEN = AE.concat(CF, TGT);
    var RTd = GIVEN.concat(["T","RT"]);
    var RUd = RTd.concat(["U","RU","angTRU","angALB"]);
    var RWd = RTd.concat(["U","RU","W","UW","WT","pRW"]);
    var XUd = RWd.concat(["X","V","d","UdSR","UWVd","dSXV","XT","sXU",
                          "pRX","pAM","pLE","pSU"]);
    var ANG = XUd.concat(["angTRU","angALB"]);
    var RTA = XUd.concat(["rtALM","rtTRS"]);
    var Yd  = XUd.concat(["Y","RY","UY","DY"]);
    var abd = Yd.concat(["a","b","ab"]);
    var Dad = abd.concat(["Da"]);
    var SOL = Dad.concat(["I","c","e","abcI","FI","Se","eY","cV","bW","de",
                          "sXY","sRI","sCI","sYI","pYc","pUV","pDT","pYT","pRF",
                          "Tb","Sd","Xc","XV","YW","eV"]);
    var HYP = GIVEN.concat(["rtALM","rtCRS"]);
    geomlib.init({
