        initiallyHidden: ["RU","UW","ab"],
        aliases: { "TR": "RT", "BE": "EB", "DF": "FD", "DR": "RD", "WU": "UW",
                   "TW": "WT", "HL": "baseAB", "RUWT": "pRW", "TD": "pDT" },
        slides: [
            { text: "“Parallelepipedal solids which are on equal bases and of the same height equal one another.”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["sAE","sCF"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "XI.31" }] },
            { text: "Let the parallelepipedal solids {AE|sAE} and {CF|sCF} of the same height be on equal bases {AB|baseAB} and {CD|baseCD}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["sAE","sCF","baseAB","baseCD"] },
            { text: "I say that the solid {AE|sAE} equals the solid {CF|sCF}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["sAE","sCF"] },
            { text: "First, let the sides which stand up, {HK}, {BE|EB}, {AG}, {LM}, {PQ}, {DF|FD}, {CO}, and {RS},",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["HK","EB","AG","LM","PQ","FD","CO","RS"] },
            { text: "be at right angles to the bases {AB|baseAB} and {CD|baseCD}.",
              visible: HYP,
              highlighted: ["baseAB","baseCD","LM","RS"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "rtALM", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "rtCRS", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "Produce the straight line {RT} in a straight line with {CR}.",
              visible: RTd,
              highlighted: ["RT","CR"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "RT", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeExtend } ] } },
            { text: "Construct the angle {TRU|angTRU} equal to the angle {ALB|angALB} at the point {R} on the straight line {RT}.",
              visible: RUd,
              highlighted: ["angTRU","angALB"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angALB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "RU", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "angTRU", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "angle TRU = angle ALB", ref: "I.23" }] },
            { text: "Make {RT} equal to A, and {RU} equal to {LB}.",
              visible: RUd,
              highlighted: ["RT","RU","LB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "RT, RU cut off", ref: "I.3" }] },
            { text: "Complete the base {RW|pRW}",
              visible: RWd,
              highlighted: ["pRW"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "UW", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "WT", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "parallels through T and U", ref: "I.31" }] },
            { text: "and the solid {XU|sXU}.",
              visible: XUd,
              highlighted: ["sXU"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "UdSR", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "UWVd", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "dSXV", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "XT", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "Now, since the two sides {TR|RT} and {RU} equal the two sides {AL} and {LB}, and they contain equal angles,",
              visible: ANG,
              highlighted: ["RT","RU","AL","LB","angTRU","angALB"] },
            { text: "therefore the parallelogram {RW|pRW} equals and is similar to the parallelogram {HL|baseAB}.",
              visible: XUd,
              highlighted: ["pRW","baseAB"] },
            { text: "Since again {AL} equals {RT}, and {LM} equals {RS}, and they contain right angles,",
              visible: RTA,
              highlighted: ["AL","RT","LM","RS"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "rtALM", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "rtTRS", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "therefore the parallelogram {RX|pRX} equals and is similar to the parallelogram {AM|pAM}.",
              visible: RTA,
              highlighted: ["pRX","pAM"] },
            { text: "For the same reason {LE|pLE} also equals and is similar to {SU|pSU}.",
              visible: XUd,
              highlighted: ["pLE","pSU"] },
            { text: "Therefore three parallelograms of the solid {AE|sAE} equal and are similar to three parallelograms of the solid {XU|sXU}.",
              visible: XUd,
              highlighted: ["baseAB","pAM","pLE","pRW","pRX","pSU"] },
            { text: "But the former three equal and are similar to the three opposite,",
              visible: XUd,
              highlighted: ["sAE"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "opposite planes equal", ref: "XI.24" }] },
            { text: "and the latter three equal and are similar the three opposite,",
              visible: XUd,
              highlighted: ["sXU"] },
            { text: "therefore the whole parallelepipedal solid {AE|sAE} equals the whole parallelepipedal solid {XU|sXU}.",
              visible: XUd,
              highlighted: ["sAE","sXU"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "solid AE = solid XU", ref: "XI.Def.10" }] },
            { text: "Draw {DR|RD} and {WU|UW} through to meet one another at {Y},",
              visible: Yd,
              highlighted: ["RD","UW","Y"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "RY", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeExtend },
                  { elem: "UY", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeExtend } ] } },
            { text: "draw {aTb|ab} through {T} parallel to {DY},",
              visible: abd,
              highlighted: ["ab","DY"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "ab", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "aTb parallel to DY", ref: "I.31" }] },
            { text: "produce {PD} to {a},",
              visible: Dad,
              highlighted: ["PD","Da"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "Da", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeExtend } ] } },
            { text: "and complete the solids {YX|sXY} and {RI|sRI}.",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sXY","sRI"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "eY", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "Se", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "de", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "bW", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "cV", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "abcI", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline },
                  { elem: "FI", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "Then the solid {XY|sXY}, of which the parallelogram {RX|pRX} is the base and {Yc|pYc} its opposite,",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sXY","pRX","pYc"] },
            { text: "equals the solid {XU|sXU}, of which the parallelogram {RX|pRX} is the base and {UV|pUV} its opposite,",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sXU","pRX","pUV"] },
            { text: "for they are on the same base {RX|pRX} and of the same height,",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["pRX"] },
            { text: "and the ends of their edges which stand up, namely {RY}, {RU}, {Tb}, {TW|WT}, {Se}, {Sd}, {Xc}, and {XV},",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["RY","RU","Tb","WT","Se","Sd","Xc","XV"] },
            { text: "are on the same straight lines {YW} and {eV}.",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["YW","eV"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "solid XY = solid XU", ref: "XI.29" }] },
            { text: "But the solid {XU|sXU} equals {AE|sAE}, therefore the solid {XY|sXY} also equals the solid {AE|sAE}.",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sXU","sAE","sXY"] },
            { text: "And, since the parallelogram {RUWT|pRW} equals the parallelogram {YT|pYT},",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["pRW","pYT"] },
            { text: "for they are on the same base {RT} and in the same parallels {RT} and {YW},",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["RT","YW"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "RUWT = YT", ref: "I.35" }] },
            { text: "and {RUWT|pRW} equals {CD|baseCD}, since it also equals {AB|baseAB},",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["pRW","baseCD","baseAB"] },
            { text: "therefore the parallelogram {YT|pYT} also equals {CD|baseCD}.",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["pYT","baseCD"] },
            { text: "But {DT|pDT} is another parallelogram, therefore the base {CD|baseCD} is to {DT|pDT} as {YT|pYT} is to {DT|pDT}.",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["pDT","baseCD","pYT"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CD : DT = YT : DT", ref: "V.7" }] },
            { text: "And, since the parallelepipedal solid {CI|sCI} is cut by the plane {RF|pRF} which is parallel to opposite planes,",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sCI","pRF"] },
            { text: "therefore the base {CD|baseCD} is to the base {DT|pDT} as the solid {CF|sCF} is to the solid {RI|sRI}.",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["baseCD","pDT","sCF","sRI"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CD : DT = solid CF : solid RI", ref: "XI.25" }] },
            { text: "For the same reason, since the parallelepipedal solid {YI|sYI} is cut by the plane {RX|pRX} which is parallel to opposite planes,",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sYI","pRX"] },
            { text: "therefore the base {YT|pYT} is to the base {TD|pDT} as the solid {YX|sXY} is to the solid {RI|sRI}.",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["pYT","pDT","sXY","sRI"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "YT : TD = solid YX : solid RI", ref: "XI.25" }] },
            { text: "But the base {CD|baseCD} is to {DT|pDT} as {YT|pYT} is to {DT|pDT},",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["baseCD","pDT","pYT"] },
            { text: "therefore the solid {CF|sCF} is to the solid {RI|sRI} as the solid {YX|sXY} is to {RI|sRI}.",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sCF","sRI","sXY"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CF : RI = YX : RI", ref: "V.11" }] },
            { text: "Therefore each of the solids {CF|sCF} and {YX|sXY} has to {RI|sRI} the same ratio.",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sCF","sXY","sRI"] },
            { text: "Therefore the solid {CF|sCF} equals the solid {YX|sXY}.",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sCF","sXY"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "solid CF = solid YX", ref: "V.9" }] },
            { text: "But {YX|sXY} was proved equal to {AE|sAE}, therefore {AE|sAE} also equals {CF|sCF}.",
              visible: SOL,
              highlighted: ["sAE","sCF"] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "XI.31") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshows' resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.3":       "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI3/",
        "I.23":      "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI23/",
        "I.31":      "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI31/",
        "I.35":      "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI35/",
        "V.7":       "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV7/",
        "V.9":       "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV9/",
        "V.11":      "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV11/",
        "XI.11":     "/elements/books/bookXI/propositions/propXI11/",
        "XI.24":     "/elements/books/bookXI/propositions/propXI24/",
        "XI.25":     "/elements/books/bookXI/propositions/propXI25/",
        "XI.29":     "/elements/books/bookXI/propositions/propXI29/",
        "XI.30":     "/elements/books/bookXI/propositions/propXI30/",
        "XI.Def.10": "/elements/books/bookXI/definitions/defXI10/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Now, since the two sides {TR|RT} and {RU} equal the two sides {AL} and {LB}, and they contain equal angles, therefore the parallelogram {RW|pRW} equals and is similar to the parallelogram {HL|baseAB}. Since again {AL} equals {RT}, and {LM} equals {RS}, and they contain right angles, therefore the parallelogram {RX|pRX} equals and is similar to the parallelogram {AM|pAM}. For the same reason {LE|pLE} also equals and is similar to {SU|pSU}.

Therefore three parallelograms of the solid {AE|sAE} equal and are similar to three parallelograms of the solid {XU|sXU}. But the former three equal and are similar to the three opposite, and the latter three equal and are similar the three opposite, therefore the whole parallelepipedal solid {AE|sAE} equals the whole parallelepipedal solid {XU|sXU}. [!just XI.24; XI.Def.10]

Draw {DR|RD} and {WU|UW} through to meet one another at {Y}, draw {aTb|ab} through {T} parallel to {DY}, produce {PD} to {a}, and complete the solids {YX|sXY} and {RI|sRI}. [!just I.31]

Then the solid {XY|sXY}, of which the parallelogram {RX|pRX} is the base and {Yc|pYc} its opposite, equals the solid {XU|sXU}, of which the parallelogram {RX|pRX} is the base and {UV|pUV} its opposite, for they are on the same base {RX|pRX} and of the same height, and the ends of their edges which stand up, namely {RY}, {RU}, {Tb}, {TW|WT}, {Se}, {Sd}, {Xc}, and {XV}, are on the same straight lines {YW} and {eV}. But the solid {XU|sXU} equals {AE|sAE}, therefore the solid {XY|sXY} also equals the solid {AE|sAE}. [!just XI.29]

And, since the parallelogram {RUWT|pRW} equals the parallelogram {YT|pYT}, for they are on the same base {RT} and in the same parallels {RT} and {YW}, and {RUWT|pRW} equals {CD|baseCD}, since it also equals {AB|baseAB}, therefore the parallelogram {YT|pYT} also equals {CD|baseCD}. [!just I.35]

But {DT|pDT} is another parallelogram, therefore the base {CD|baseCD} is to {DT|pDT} as {YT|pYT} is to {DT|pDT}. [!just V.7]

And, since the parallelepipedal solid {CI|sCI} is cut by the plane {RF|pRF} which is parallel to opposite planes, therefore the base {CD|baseCD} is to the base {DT|pDT} as the solid {CF|sCF} is to the solid {RI|sRI}. For the same reason, since the parallelepipedal solid {YI|sYI} is cut by the plane {RX|pRX} which is parallel to opposite planes, therefore the base {YT|pYT} is to the base {TD|pDT} as the solid {YX|sXY} is to the solid {RI|sRI}. [!just XI.25]

But the base {CD|baseCD} is to {DT|pDT} as {YT|pYT} is to {DT|pDT}, therefore the solid {CF|sCF} is to the solid {RI|sRI} as the solid {YX|sXY} is to {RI|sRI}. [!just V.11]

Therefore each of the solids {CF|sCF} and {YX|sXY} has to {RI|sRI} the same ratio. Therefore the solid {CF|sCF} equals the solid {YX|sXY}. But {YX|sXY} was proved equal to {AE|sAE}, therefore {AE|sAE} also equals {CF|sCF}. [!just V.9]

<hr width="50%">

Next, let the sides standing up, {AG:canvas_1}, {HK:canvas_1}, {BE|EB:canvas_1}, {LM:canvas_1}, {CN:canvas_1}, {PQ:canvas_1}, {DF|FD:canvas_1}, and {RS:canvas_1}, not be at right angles to the bases {AB|baseAB:canvas_1} and {CD|baseCD:canvas_1}.

I say again that the solid {AE|sAE:canvas_1} equals the solid {CF|sCF:canvas_1}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_1" width="400" height="280" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XI.31 diagram" src="propXI31b.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // The second case: the standing sides oblique. Perpendiculars from the
    // eight upper corners meet the plane of reference at O, T, U, V, W, X,
